  {"a": "Rollo", "e": "His descendants ruled Normandy, and one of them took England in 1066.", "p": "Which Viking leader was given the French land that became Normandy?", "s": "vikings", "w": ["Ragnar", "Harald", "Sweyn"]},
  {"a": "Homage", "p": "What was it called when a vassal knelt and swore loyalty?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["Tribute", "Penance", "Tithing"]},
  {"a": "One tenth", "e": "This church due was called the tithe, a word that simply means a tenth.", "p": "What share of his crop did a peasant usually owe the church?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["One quarter", "One third", "One half"]},
  {"a": "Fallow", "e": "Resting a field let the soil recover, since there was no fertiliser to buy.", "p": "What did farmers call a field left unplanted for a year?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["Pasture", "Meadow", "Furrow"]},
  {"a": "The demesne", "p": "What was the lord's own farmland on a manor called?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["The commons", "The meadow", "The glebe"]},
  {"a": "The horse collar", "e": "It moved the weight to the shoulders, so horses slowly replaced oxen in the fields.", "p": "Which invention let a horse pull a heavy plough without choking?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["The horseshoe", "The stirrup", "The saddle"]},
  {"a": "At the lord's mill", "e": "The lord kept a share of the flour as payment, which villagers often resented.", "p": "Where did peasants usually have to grind their grain?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["At the town market", "At the church door", "At the river bank"]},
  {"a": "Corvée", "e": "Scutage was money a knight paid instead of going to war.", "p": "What was the unpaid work a peasant owed his lord called?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["Tallage", "Scutage", "Tithe"]},
  {"a": "Mud and sticks", "e": "Builders wove sticks together and packed them with mud and straw, called wattle and daub.", "p": "What were the walls of a peasant's cottage usually made of?", "s": "feudal_life", "w": ["Fired clay bricks", "Cut stone blocks", "Sawn oak planks"]},
